Optimal Solution - Fast exponentiation using divide-and-conquer to compute power in logarithmic time.
                   Use binary exponentiation: square the base and halve the power to reduce time complexity from linear to logarithmic.

class Solution {
    public double myPow(double x, int n) {
        // Convert n to long to safely handle Integer.MIN_VALUE
        return solve(x, (long) n);
    }
    public double solve(double x, long n) {
        // Base case: x^0 = 1
        if (n == 0)
            return 1;
        // If power is negative, convert to reciprocal
        if (n < 0)
            return solve(1 / x, -n);
        // If n is even, use exponentiation by squaring
        if (n % 2 == 0)
            return solve(x * x, n / 2);
        // If n is odd, multiply once by x and reduce the problem
        return x * solve(x * x, (n - 1) / 2);
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(log n).
Space Complexity :- O(log n).
